          }
        },
        "1658930183f010c50f-1": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What is diecast made of?",
            "answer": "<p>A diecast model is a miniature replica created through the die casting or metal casting process. These scale models are usually made of zinc or lead alloy and come fully formed as a single piece that depicts the real vehicle in small scale.</p>"
          }
        },
        "1658930183f010c50f-2": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Can diecast be painted?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes! Many hobbyists enjoy repainting existing diecast models with various techniques such as airbrushing and spray painting. </p>"
          }
        },
        "1658930183f010c50f-3": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Are diecast cars worth anything?",
            "answer": "<p>Diecast model cars increase in value, especially if they are well-made, accurate, and durable. The value of diecast cars is determined by a variety of factors, including their size, brand, availability, trends, and condition.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
